---
import Doc from '../layouts/Doc.astro';
import SiteLink from '../components/SiteLink.astro';
import { APP_NAME, BUSINESS_NAME, SUPPORT_EMAIL } from '../utils/env';

const effectiveDateISO = '2026-04-20';
const effectiveDateLabel = 'April 20, 2026';
---

<Doc
  title="Privacy"
  description={`How ${APP_NAME} handles data. Anonymous usage data via TelemetryDeck, nothing else.`}
>
  <header class="doc__header">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
  </header>

  <p>
    We can't see your drawings. {APP_NAME} has no server of its own,
    which means your drawings and game progress travel directly from
    your phone to your friend's inside the iMessage you send, while
    Apple handles any in-app purchases. The only thing that reaches
    us is anonymous usage data that helps us make the game better,
    described below.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>
      We use TelemetryDeck to collect anonymous usage data. Under GDPR,
      our basis is Art. 6(1)(f) legitimate interest, because we need a
      reliable way to understand how the app gets used.
    </p>
    <p>Data transferred:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>An anonymized, untraceable user ID (per app installation).</li>
      <li>Actions defined by the app publisher (for example, "app launched," "settings opened").</li>
      <li>Rounded timestamps (nearest hour).</li>
      <li>Device metadata (system and app version, device type).</li>
      <li>Publisher-defined metadata.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Data not collected:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>No IP addresses (not in logs, not in the database).</li>
      <li>No cookies or tracking technologies.</li>
      <li>No persistent identifiers that could be traced back to individuals.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How we use it</h2>
    <p>
      We look at this data to see which features get used, find bugs,
      and make the app better, and that's the whole list. We don't run
      ads, build user profiles, or sell data to anyone.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Drawings and reports</h2>
    <p>
      Your drawings go directly to the people you send them to through
      iMessage, so we're not in the middle at any point. If a word the
      app gave you looks wrong or offensive, tap Report on it and a
      pre-filled email lands with us for review. If you want to stop
      hearing from a specific player, use iMessage's block feature.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Payments</h2>
    <p>
      We never see your payment info, because Apple handles any in-app
      purchases under <SiteLink
        href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/"
        target="_blank"
        aria-label="Apple's privacy policy, opens in new tab"
      >Apple's privacy policy</SiteLink>&#8288;.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Who handles the data</h2>
    <p>
      TelemetryDeck GmbH handles this data, based in Germany
      (Von-der-Tann-Str. 54, 86159 Augsburg). Their privacy policy
      lives at <SiteLink
        href="https://telemetrydeck.com/privacy"
        target="_blank"
        aria-label="TelemetryDeck privacy policy, opens in new tab"
      >telemetrydeck.com/privacy</SiteLink>&#8288;, and they're held
      to the same standard this page describes.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Keeping and deleting data</h2>
    <p>
      The data we collect is anonymous, so there's no personal record
      of you sitting around for us to keep or delete. If you'd rather
      have it off entirely, the app has an Analytics toggle, and once
      you turn it off nothing else gets sent.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Your GDPR rights</h2>
    <p>
      Under GDPR, you have the right to access, correct, or object to
      the processing of personal data that relates to you. The catch
      with this app is that the data above can't be traced back to a
      person, so in most cases there's no record tied to you, and if
      we can't find one we'll say so.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Do Not Track</h2>
    <p>This app does not track your online activities across third-party websites or services.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>
      {APP_NAME} isn't aimed at children under 13, and we don't
      knowingly collect information from them.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>If this page changes</h2>
    <p>
      When something important here changes, we'll update the effective
      date below and show a notice inside the app before the change
      takes effect.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Questions?</h2>
    <p>
      Email <SiteLink href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</SiteLink>&#8288; with
      questions about this policy. {BUSINESS_NAME} runs the app and
      maintains this page.
    </p>
  </section>

  <footer class="doc__meta">Effective <time datetime={effectiveDateISO}>{effectiveDateLabel}</time></footer>
</Doc>
